A||||8||fierohoho||Pop-Rivet Tool Question||||1||
Z||000000||fierohoho||11-13-2001||05:38 AM||||Who sells one or what brand name tool is there that will handle the big rivets like on the doors and body of the Fiero?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||revin||11-13-2001||07:23 AM||||I wish I knew! What I did was went to Pep Boys (auto parts store) and they had some "big washer" rivets in a 3/16 size. they worked very well for me when I had to put the ground effects back on.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||11-13-2001||07:36 AM||||an auto body supply store/paint store. also some of the traveling vendors like "MAC" or "Snap ON" tool trucks. There not cheap. Maybe someone has one theyd be willing to lend you.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||11-13-2001||08:01 AM||||I think Harbor Frieght has/had then for around $20||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||11-13-2001||08:19 AM||||I bought the Marson Kit. It has the tool and 80 rivets in 4 different sizes. Including the big head rivets. I bought the kit from a body shop/paint supply store. The cost was $44.95. The Marson Kit # is 48001.<P>More info at: <A HREF="http://www.marsoncorp.com" TARGET=_blank>www.marsoncorp.com</A> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.marsoncorp.com/images/48001.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroluke||11-13-2001||08:37 AM||||HI<P>Don't confuse the plastic riveter with the big riveter you need for the aluminum rivets.<P>These are the rivets for the fenders, rocker panels, etc.<P>I got mine from Tools USA, but it was not cheap; this is a huge riveter. I think it was<BR>called "Big Daddy" or something...<P>Best regards,<P>-Oliver||||reg||4
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||11-13-2001||10:30 AM||||Oliver, Yes it's the "Big Daddy" I have one also. $125.00 I think it was?   <P>It is a Marson Big Daddy PN. 39031<P><BR>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierohoho||11-13-2001||10:51 AM||||I'm pretty sure the Marson"Big Daddy" is what I'm looking for, thanks guys, HoHo.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||11-13-2001||11:41 AM||||I used one from Harbor Freight that cost less than $30 I think (Wolfhound loan). Do a search in the Mall. I removed all the panels in my car except the roof and rear top. I only needed big rivets for attaching inside supports for rocker panels (aero). The rest I did easily with threaded rivets ($16 at HF).<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
